{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:48:07Z","created_by_operation":"op_24d5d3610e46405b9718b67f7d7a6b2b","id":"pg_ebcc38c682465d27b31c1c334b70f887","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/doucs91-hivelore-conventions-md-f6ddcc78c4fe-1c334b70f887.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_dd28406c3c0e5028b77d8cf53d36e798"],"title":"Doucs91/hivelore/CONVENTIONS.md @ f6ddcc78c4fe","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:48:07Z","updated_by_operation":"op_24d5d3610e46405b9718b67f7d7a6b2b"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_08b051410b81e793da92b4ee2957cc85dc94d0d8dd65281ab677bfd0656d4d0b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"MCP tool exposure is controlled by a profile variable: enforcement (default), maintenance, and experimental/full as legacy aliases for maintenance after the experimental diagnostics were removed in v0.32.0."},{"claim_ids":["clm_23b30b81b8025409e7b0705e222c0ec546ee7ef38befb2c4fb369a6ab493d941"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Memory verbs mirror MCP tool names across CLI and MCP (save/search/get/delete ↔ mem_save/mem_search/mem_get/mem_delete), with older add/query/show/rm aliases still working."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2830a97721f29189e00c310e09a035f2e4e8cf1ea98d3e016367fdc1498aa979"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Only deterministic, code-bound evidence can block a commit (validated sensors, anchored anti-patterns, stale anchors on touched files); anchor, literal-token, and semantic matches are surfaced for review, never blocked."},{"claim_ids":["clm_436e7356c3fad348111d274b9ad67c70d222a5eab4a9fdf37ea95f28a3098404"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Since v0.57.0 anchor matches are weighted by path rarity (IDF): anchors touched by over 35% of recent commits need corroboration to outrank others, and too-small samples are reported as unknown and rank as before."},{"claim_ids":["clm_55677261abc0c96447a1e50f5478317544b8dce488de4134b7a93de2b0b294ef"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The monorepo contains @hivelore/cli (main product), @hivelore/mcp (bundled MCP server), @hivelore/core (types, schema, anchors, token budgets), @hivelore/embeddings (optional offline semantic ranking), plus a VS Code extension and a GitHub Action."},{"claim_ids":["clm_57a8e60a48ec47a0d8a0be6b2b26906c6307de537130f9fb26695b6104e43f45"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Knowledge lives as Git-native Markdown records (decision, gotcha, convention, attempt, architecture) under .ai/, anchored to file paths and symbols; team memories are committed to git while personal memories and runtime/cache state are gitignored."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6ec40cca31ae0aa4f3a361ebc5d88e46217a9c900317949432e85a6102164831"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI requires Node >= 20 and is published as @hivelore/cli on npm; ast-grep sensors need the optional @ast-grep/napi engine, and semantic search needs the optional @hivelore/embeddings package (~110MB model)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7fb09af8086175b05cb6c0cff2194ef7542b4be1e47482e62fdc4513a347c201"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Sensors follow a validation doctrine of silent on correct code and firing on the mistake; autogenerated sensors start as warn and humans promote vetted ones to block, and inverted patterns matching the lesson's own fix are refused."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8ad5802dd396d693c5feb044e107703d819555a30dd71dda04a0c8568a6bfa98"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Enforcement is governed by a single posture knob (advisory, balanced default, strict); process gates never refuse a local commit at any posture, and strict adds process gates at pre-push and CI."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9e27054cdcb8dcf343bfb8ce99a92274c2c4b676c064c4be0d353f33bb4e9aba"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product ships an MCP server exposing tools including get_briefing, mem_save, mem_tried, mem_search, mem_get, mem_update, propose_sensor, code_map, code_search, mem_verify, scaffold_test, and pre_commit_check."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d93f83f9f9bda96536d4fa04456a469478a1cc70f3554db8081c9b6991e28a6b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README states Hivelore does not verify functional correctness or replace tests, linters, security scanners, or LLM evals; command sensors only route the team's own tests as oracles, a partial static slice of behaviour control."},{"claim_ids":["clm_da5a1085d8cd842e6e3e5e89e38f6f2a44ce4d7a5ecce45259f9d4321057ae6e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI offers commands including init, doctor, agent setup, briefing, memory save/tried/search/get, sensors check/propose/promote, enforce install/status/check/ci/finish, sync, session end, ingest, and index."}],"claim_ids":["clm_08b051410b81e793da92b4ee2957cc85dc94d0d8dd65281ab677bfd0656d4d0b","clm_23b30b81b8025409e7b0705e222c0ec546ee7ef38befb2c4fb369a6ab493d941","clm_2830a97721f29189e00c310e09a035f2e4e8cf1ea98d3e016367fdc1498aa979","clm_436e7356c3fad348111d274b9ad67c70d222a5eab4a9fdf37ea95f28a3098404","clm_55677261abc0c96447a1e50f5478317544b8dce488de4134b7a93de2b0b294ef","clm_57a8e60a48ec47a0d8a0be6b2b26906c6307de537130f9fb26695b6104e43f45","clm_6ec40cca31ae0aa4f3a361ebc5d88e46217a9c900317949432e85a6102164831","clm_7fb09af8086175b05cb6c0cff2194ef7542b4be1e47482e62fdc4513a347c201","clm_8ad5802dd396d693c5feb044e107703d819555a30dd71dda04a0c8568a6bfa98","clm_9e27054cdcb8dcf343bfb8ce99a92274c2c4b676c064c4be0d353f33bb4e9aba","clm_d93f83f9f9bda96536d4fa04456a469478a1cc70f3554db8081c9b6991e28a6b","clm_da5a1085d8cd842e6e3e5e89e38f6f2a44ce4d7a5ecce45259f9d4321057ae6e"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:48:07Z","created_by_operation":"op_24d5d3610e46405b9718b67f7d7a6b2b","id":"pg_ec95b107b6b95eb6897a6b430fcf515b","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/doucs91-hivelore-readme-md-f6ddcc78c4fe-6b430fcf515b.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_94ce43533247585197669b2c74b96d8e"],"title":"Doucs91/hivelore/README.md @ f6ddcc78c4fe","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:48:07Z","updated_by_operation":"op_24d5d3610e46405b9718b67f7d7a6b2b"}
